I've uploaded version 1.6b of Mumail to the various linux ftp sites
(tsx-11, sunsite, and nic) as well as the program's home, sipb.mit.edu:
/pub/seyon/MUMAIL.  

Mumail is an X-based mail reader. Though it had a humble beginnings,
it's grown into a full-featured monster -- just about anything you can
think of is there (including a decent kitchen sink :->). It has the best
features of mh, elm, vm, and Supercite. It's user-frienly, and fun to
use (yes, even a Mac-like animated cursor!). It reads/writes elm folders
since it uses the mailbox format.

If you get c.o.l by mail, or subscribe to one of the activists mailing
lists, Mumail has support of bursting digests into constituent letters
-- much more convientient to browse and reply or follow-up to. This
version even handles compressed/gzipped folders trasparently, so you can
go back and search old archived folders for a letter you thought you'd
never come back to.

Anyways, enough of the publicity. If you use it and like it, let me
know. If you hate it... well, it didn't cost you anything now did it?

Enjoy!

-- M. Saggaf



