I have uploaded a LinuX port of bibcard, written by ogden@nmsu.edu. Bibcard 
is an OpenLook interface to BibTeX databases. You can find the file on
tsx-11.mit.edu and sunsite.unc.edu.

To run bibcard, you need libxv3.so.2, libolg.so.3, libX11.so.3 and
libc.so.4 . The bibcard files should be installed in the following
directories:

	bibcard -> /usr/TeX/bin/bibcard  (or where you have your TeX related
					  bin files)
	bibcard.1 -> /usr/man/man1
	bt.info   -> $OPENWINHOME/help

The source code is included, beside bt_ex.c, there was nothing to do!!
bt_ex.c.org is the original file (I think it is for Sun's). 

Bibcard searches for bibliography files in the current directory, or in 
directories that are named by the BIBPATH environment variable.

Be careful with databases with more than 400 entries, you will need MUCH
memory.

